A||||11||Brian84SE||Auto trans shift kit||||1||
Z||000000||Brian84SE||03-04-2000||09:02 PM||||Fiero store has a shift kit for the TH 125.<BR>Does anyone have any experience with how good this is?   Is it easy to install? I get a little nervous messing around with auto transmission valve bodys....I picture ball bearings and springs going everywhere!!||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||03-04-2000||09:18 PM||||I do not recomend a novice install a "shift kit." It's not just a simple issue of dropping on a few parts. It depends on the exact kit just what's involved. Fiero Store won't say where they get theirs.<P>Every kit I've ever seen requires droping the valve body. While that usually doesn't mean parts going every place, it's nothing to take lightly.<P>There are a bunch of small parts in there. if you put one into someplace it didn't belong then you've got a real problem.<P>Shift kits usually consist of some springs, some steel balls, and in the case of B&M sometimes a new seperator plate.<P>If you think your TH125c is shifting baddly then you need to find out exactly why. Sticking a shift kit into a tranny with a problem can be a very bad thing. Often in TH125c something as small as a 2-3,000th error in the TV cable adjustment is enought to really screw them up.<P>Also, doing just a filter & fluid on TH125c can make a major dif. The new DexronIII is signifigantly better than the DII was that the tranny was originally run with. Trick here is to get out as much of the old fluid as posible. ((It's postible to remove over 6 quarts. Without dropping the tranny, and without a TC drain plug.)) ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||03-05-2000||01:25 AM||||I bought my shift kit thru IRM many moons ago it came in a B&M box.I don't know if they still sell it or not. I thought the Fiero store was a "Trans Pak" brand but don't know for sure. I had a friend at a trans shop install it due to the "bag of parts" it came with. So I cannot comment on how hard it would be to do. But I can tell you that on mine it shifts normally when cruising but at WOT the gears slam Hard and the feeling of being pushed into the seat is great! As for real perfomance numbers I have none. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jim Baumann||03-05-2000||01:46 AM||||Is there a big difference between Dextron II & III and is it bad to mix them?||||reg||5
Z||000004||GREENDANO||03-05-2000||10:15 AM||||The Fiero Store's shift kit is a Trans-Go/Trans Star kit.  Very complete, not just a shift kit, but a trans improvement kit.  I've done two now in my Fieros.  Definately not a beginner project, but not too complicated that with a manual and a little patience it can be done in an afternoon.<BR>  Dan-O||||reg||1
Z||000005||87SC/GT||03-05-2000||10:28 AM||||Northern Auto parts has the Trans-Go kit. I think it was only about 20.00 for the th125 kit.        <A HREF="http://www.naparts.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.naparts.com/</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||03-05-2000||10:37 AM||||Dexron 2& 3 can be mixed. you loose the effectivness of the Dexron 3 improvments if there's allot of 2 left.<P>Transmission Exchange caries Transgo kits as well as anything else the tranny might need.<P>I recomend highly that the TC lock solinoid be replaced if your draining the tranny anyway. It's cheap. It's one less thing to break later.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 03-05-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||DaRkLoRD||03-05-2000||03:27 PM||||$20.00??<P>If they're that cheap, I'll get one for sure.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I've heard a bit about shift kits, but never thought about how much they cost.. I'd get a transmission shop to install it tho, as my experience with modifying engines might not even cover adding a K&N filter.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>(never tried it, but I think I could figure it out.)||||reg||1
