Z||000011||Capt Fiero||03-06-2000||07:01 PM||||The one thing that I do not see mentiond hear is that when installing a shift kit into a Fiero, it is a pain.  I can not comment on all kits.  But the one that I have seen used, requires you to remove a plate on the side of the tranny, not just the pan and valve body.  When trying to do a shift kit it is very hard to do it in the car.  Near impossible.  I am going to install a shift kit into my spare tranny before installing it with my rebuilt engine.  Shift kits are cheap (20-50$) and do improve both power and engine operation.  A bad analgy is it makes you car more like a stick shift.  Gives you harder faster shifts. (no you do not have to shift it manually) it just shifts harder like a stick.  You have to admit the 125C after warm up, shifts more like a wet noodle than anything else.<BR>||||reg||1
